title Five reds from one clone; the ledger's headline becomes a number the tool writes
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Rota row 1 by lap index. git rev-list --count HEAD read 3446 at the open, so 3446 mod 5 = 1 -- Air and Saturn, law and boundary: TAME_CORE, single-stranded, and Gauge Style which loads every lap anyway. Single-stranded governed the shape twice over. Its test is whether a part can be drawn out and understood alone, and the pre-commit hook's two rules are exactly that: two triggers, two pages, one shared refresh function, each readable without the other. Row 3, Water and Venus, has now gone unread three transitions running under the commit-count reading, so it was read as a make-up -- the happy zone and the thin edge, whose mirrored-pair argument is what the headline writer and its reader now form at the ledger's own seam.
think The cold roster opened on 61 guards, 56 green, 5 red, and Standfast books the remainder of the journey to reds. Every one of the five traces to two commits of the 20260825.180329 lap, which ran on the macOS clone and never read the roster. b812a1c24f took construction/ITINERARY.md from 24,560 to 26,469 bytes against the 24,576 its header declares and wrote a Git nib of bc5bd1f902, the pre-amend hash of that same commit, which exists in one machine's object store and resolves nowhere here. 5b94dd2d69 booked row %225, took construction/REDS.md from 24,057 to 26,187 against the same bound, and left the headline reciting 224 against a measured 225. One index row stood at 215 bytes against 192.
think Four roots rather than five symptoms. The pins and the index row are ordinary accretion the fold discipline handles. The nib is a machine-local hash the seated convention produces by construction. The headline is arithmetic a hand was still republishing, and that is the third firing -- REDS %127 and %141 are the same fault, both closed by hand.
think The sharpest finding came from planning a different lap. tools/r/remember_git_nib_witness.rish was written as the loom after the nib class fired twice as %103 and %106, and its own header names the exact flaw that bit here. It sits in the unreached band: no roster row reaches it by any path, so the guard built for this fault ran on no lap. REDS %224 seated the unreached gate one lap earlier and its 1,202 read as an abstraction; this is the first member of that band whose absence cost a round.
think The repair for the headline is the fourth rung of the ladder %223 names. Rule was %141 -- a row and its headline are one edit. Reading is reds_ledger_headline_scan.sh. Refusal is the next lap's cold roster. Where a value is arithmetic there is one rung past refusal, which is to remove the hand: the tool that measures the spine writes the three numbers, and the commit that books a row refreshes them.
think The nib was pinned to HEAD rather than to the pre-amend sibling this round, which is one of the three states the loom already accepts and the only one that resolves on every clone. Changing the seated convention stays Keaton's word and is surfaced in %227 rather than crossed.
obs REDS %226, %227, %228 booked and closed. Rows %223-%225 folded to their own shelf, and 23 of the pin's 26 fold-pointer lines moved to the recital shelf that already holds their elders -- 9,540 bytes of pointers stood against 6,684 bytes of rows, rising about 370 bytes a round, so every round had come to need a fold. The pin reads 16,693 and the card 24,548, both under 24,576.
obs The writer is proven from both sides on planted ledgers rather than only in the writing direction: the repair, the shelf-spanning count, idempotence, check mode writing nothing, a headline-less ledger refused by name, the rows byte-identical across a repair, and the tracked mode surviving the in-place rewrite. Seven behaviors, and three more on the hook's own control, which now stands at eight.
obs This row's own headline was written by the tool -- the loom closed the red it was built for, in the same round, on the ledger it guards.
obs Two roster rows landed: remember_git_nib and reds_ledger_headline, 63 guards to 65.
